        en: "Ljubostinja Monastery is a masterpiece of the Morava school of architecture, founded at the end of the 14th century by Princess Milica. As a nunnery, it is renowned for its refined ornamental stone carvings and frescoes that perfectly reflect the aesthetic values of that era. Nestled within a picturesque natural setting, the monastery has persisted through the centuries as a vital spiritual and cultural center for the surrounding region. Arts K7 — medieval religious architecture and iconography." 
