    descriptionAdvancedEn: "Oplenac is the historic hill in Topola that serves as the site for the mausoleum of the Karađorđević royal family, marking a location of immense historical and artistic importance for Serbia. The Church of Saint George, situated atop this hill, is internationally famous for its spectacular mosaics, which are composed of millions of colored glass tiles to create an interior of overwhelming beauty. The mausoleum serves as the final resting place for members of the royal family and remains a powerful symbol of Serbian national identity. History K8 — royal heritage and national history.",
